      "title": "ieee80211: Add an address null check",
      "message": "ieee80211: Add an address null check\n\nThe EAPOL decryption code must not assume that the BSSID and STA address\nare both present. In addition to fuzzed data, this applies to Bluetooth\nAMP which always sends data packets with the ToDS and FromDS bits in the FCF\nset to one, and hence the addresses are not interpreted as BSSID and STA\nand BSSID_KEY and STA_KEY are not present on the packet.\n\nSee Volume 5 of\nhttps://www.bluetooth.com/specifications/specs/core-specification-amended-5-2/\nand issue #7633.\n\nNote that Bluetooth AMP was removed in v5.3:\nhttps://www.bluetooth.com/wp-content/uploads/2021/01/Bluetooth_5.3_Feature_Enhancements_Update.pdf\ndue to low adoption rates, but is v5.2 is scheduled for deprecation in\n2032 and withdrawal in 2035.\n\nIt's not clear that decryption properly works on Bluetooth AMP if the\nkey is available, but at least don't crash.\n\nFix #20565\n",
